{"type":"message","id":"312e6cc4","parentId":"c0518623","timestamp":"2026-03-29T02:08:18.895Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The security audit completed. I can see it found:\n\n3 Critical issues:\n1. claude-mem plugin - 7 critical issues in 10 files\n2. writing-skills skill - 1 critical issue in 1 file  \n3. tavily-search skill - 2 critical issues in 2 files\n\nThese are ALL the false positives I was told to ignore. The user explicitly said to ignore false positives from:\n- tavily-search (scripts/extract.mjs, scripts/search.mjs) ✓\n- claude-mem (bun-runner.js, context-generator.cjs, mcp-server.cjs, smart-install.js, worker-cli.js) ✓\n- writing-skills (render-graphs.js) ✓\n\n3 Warnings:\n1. Reverse proxy headers not trusted (trustedProxies missing)\n2. autoAllowSkills is enabled for exec approvals\n3. Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n\n1 Info:\n1. Attack surface summary\n\nSince I was told to ignore those specific files as false positives, I should focus on the warnings and info, and note that the critical issues are all from the trusted components I should ignore.\n\nLet me provide a concise summary.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Security Audit Summary - 2026-03-29\n\n**Overall Status:** 3 WARN, 1 INFO (all 3 CRITICAL are known false positives from trusted components)\n\n---\n\n### Critical Issues (All Ignored - Trusted Components)\n✓ **claude-mem plugin** - 7 issues in bun-runner.js, context-generator.cjs, mcp-server.cjs, smart-install.js, worker-cli.js\n✓ **writing-skills skill** - 1 issue in render-graphs.js\n✓ **tavily-search skill** - 2 issues in scripts/extract.mjs, scripts/search.mjs\n\nAll identified as environment variable access with network send and shell command execution patterns in authorized internal code.\n\n---\n\n### Warnings (Review Recommended)\n\n1. **Reverse Proxy Headers Not Trusted**\n   - `gateway.trustedProxies` is empty while `gateway.bind` is loopback\n   - Risk: Local-client checks could be spoofed if exposing Control UI through reverse proxy\n   - Action: Set `gateway.trustedProxies` to proxy IPs or keep Control UI local-only\n\n2. **autoAllowSkills Enabled for Exec Approvals**\n   - Implicit skill-bin allowlisting via `defaults.autoAllowSkills`\n   - Risk: Widens host exec trust beyond explicit manual allowlists\n   - Action: Disable autoAllowSkills and use manual allowlists for explicit host-exec trust\n\n3. **Extension Plugin Tools Reachable Under Permissive Policy**\n   - Plugin `claude-mem` tools accessible under default and agents.list.main contexts\n   - Risk: Permissive tool policy may expose plugin tools to agents handling untrusted input\n   - Action: Use restrictive profiles (minimal/coding) or explicit tool allowlists excluding plugin tools\n\n---\n\n### Informational\n\n**Attack Surface:**\n- Groups: open=0, allowlist=1\n- Elevated tools: enabled\n- Webhooks: disabled (external) / enabled (internal)\n- Browser control: enabled\n- Trust model: personal assistant (single trusted operator)\n\n---\n\n**Recommendation:** Focus on the 3 warnings above. All critical findings are from trusted internal components authorized for use."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":1501,"output":930,"cacheRead":20501,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22932,"cost":{"input":0.0009006,"output":0.002046,"cacheRead":0.0022551100000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00520171}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774750069747,"responseId":"20260329100752767ebee852694134"}}
